=== (b) DRIFT + SELF-HEAL within one reconcile tick ===
    A stale/edited snapshot is pushed OUT OF BAND (SIGUSR1 --push-raw),
    a VALID config that is NOT the Git desired (env=drifted). node-a
    binds it, so its DELIVERED record now diverges from Git desired
    (the delivered != desired truth-table row; the node re-ACKs desired
    before its next heartbeat, so observed == desired at heal time).
--- node-a drifted: bound the out-of-band snapshot, then healed back ---
[2026-08-01T18:05:05Z INFO  gatewayd::client] [cp-client] node "node-a" ACK v2 (swapped local cfg v1->v2, bound_hash=b8934000979d)
[2026-08-01T18:05:06Z INFO  gatewayd::client] [cp-client] node "node-a" ACK v3 (swapped local cfg v2->v3, bound_hash=55b752fc24ee)
--- reconciler: three-hash compare (desired/delivered/observed) + heal ---
[2026-08-01T18:05:05Z INFO  gatewayctl] [inject] SIGUSR1: distributing raw snapshot demo/drift-snapshot.yaml (1399 bytes), BYPASSING the render gate — nodes are the validation authority
[2026-08-01T18:05:06Z WARN  gatewayctl::reconcile] [reconcile] node "node-a" delivery stale (delivered != desired): desired=55b752fc24ee delivered=b8934000979d observed=55b752fc24ee; self-healing by re-pushing desired
[2026-08-01T18:05:06Z INFO  gatewayctl::reconcile] [reconcile] node "node-a" healed back to desired render_hash=55b752fc24ee
[2026-08-01T18:05:06Z INFO  gatewayctl::reconcile] [reconcile] tick: in_sync=0 healed=1 break_glass=0 divergent=0 unknown=0 mid_rollout=0 pending_later_wave=0
    ^ the reconciler DETECTED the delivered != desired divergence and
      RE-PUSHED desired; node-a swapped back and ACKed — healed (docs/07:
      self-heal is re-push). The observed != desired row (node running a
      stale local file) is covered in tests/reconcile.rs.

=== (c) BREAK-GLASS with TTL: tolerate the drift, then heal after expiry ===
    node-a is marked break-glass for 4s (SIGUSR2), THEN drifted again
    (out-of-band push). The reconciler must TOLERATE — not fight — the
    drift while the window is open, then heal once the TTL lapses.
--- while break-glass is OPEN: reconciler TOLERATES the drift (no heal) ---
[2026-08-01T18:05:09Z INFO  gatewayctl] [break-glass] node "node-a" marked break-glass for 4s (until unix 1785607513); the reconciler will tolerate its drift until then (docs/00)
[2026-08-01T18:05:10Z INFO  gatewayctl::reconcile] [reconcile] node "node-a" is BREAK-GLASS (override until unix 1785607513); tolerating its drift, NOT healing (docs/00 break-glass with TTL)
[2026-08-01T18:05:12Z INFO  gatewayctl::reconcile] [reconcile] node "node-a" is BREAK-GLASS (override until unix 1785607513); tolerating its drift, NOT healing (docs/00 break-glass with TTL)
--- after the TTL LAPSES: reconciler resumes and heals node-a to desired ---
[2026-08-01T18:05:14Z WARN  gatewayctl::reconcile] [reconcile] node "node-a" delivery stale (delivered != desired): desired=55b752fc24ee delivered=b8934000979d observed=55b752fc24ee; self-healing by re-pushing desired
[2026-08-01T18:05:14Z INFO  gatewayctl::reconcile] [reconcile] node "node-a" healed back to desired render_hash=55b752fc24ee
[2026-08-01T18:05:14Z INFO  gatewayctl::reconcile] [reconcile] tick: in_sync=0 healed=1 break_glass=0 divergent=0 unknown=0 mid_rollout=0 pending_later_wave=0

=== (d) ADMISSION BLOCKS A BAD CONFIG (CI gate on a config PR) ===
    A candidate config PR strips the attribution key from the route
    (violates GB-1). 'gatewayctl admit' must BLOCK it and exit non-zero,
    so it can never become desired / never roll out.
BLOCK: dir:/tmp/tmp.VB6bGWIzvi/config-repo failed admission:
  - [GB-1] route "/openai" has no effective attribution required_keys — every route must enforce at least one attribution key (GB-1)
    admit exit code: 1 (non-zero => blocked, CI fails the PR)

--- and the GOOD Git HEAD the fleet actually runs admits (exit 0) ---
ADMIT: git:/tmp/tmp.lu4iwJkuGx/config-repo@HEAD passed all admission rules
    admit exit code: 0 (zero => admitted)

